<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese bonds ended the week on a firm note, supported by the possibility that the lira might return to the EU's exchange rate mechanism.</p>
<p>Dealers said three- and five-year maturities would gain next week while 10-year bonds would continue to track Spanish Bonos closely.</p>
<p>The yield spread over 10-year German Bunds was likely to remain at around 125 basis points, they said.</p>
<p>The escudo closed stronger against the mark, buoyed by the lira news. It finished at 101.00/05 per mark after opening at 101.07/10.</p>
<p>-- LISBON BUREAU 3511-3538254</p>
</text>
